  "body": "The post-merge batch gate on main is red in the app suites. Run 43723593734 (head 6f8b309dc) shows two new failures. Evidence is in the comment on #1909 (issuecomment 6896561761).\n\n## Failures\n\n1. `troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources` in `crates/app/tests/docs_troubleshooting.rs:83`.\n   - The test reads `site/content/guide/troubleshooting.md`.\n   - PR #1908 (commit 89b43e04d, \"fix(docs): group the user guide by job stage\") moved the page to `site/content/guide/reference/troubleshooting.md`.\n   - The path in the test is now wrong.\n2. `threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit` in `crates/app/tests/operations.rs:1433`.\n   - The test panics on a create or generate `expect`.\n   - The fixture creates an APocket3D operation.\n   - Suspect: PR #1895 (commit 5adf0114d, \"fix(3d): refuse pocket depths beyond tool assembly reach\", issue #1844). The new reach refusal can refuse the fixture.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Point test 1 at the new path of the page.\n- Find the cause of failure 2. If the refusal is correct for the fixture, change the fixture so that the test again compares the threaded batch with the serial loop. Do not weaken the refusal. If the refusal is wrong, report it as a defect of #1895.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe two tests pass on main.\n",
